Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 00:05:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 5/7] cherry-pick PR 25229 (incremental namespace sync)

Squashed from upstream argoproj/argo-cd#25229 (still open, base master
46ffedca2) plus our review fix locking the namespaceCancels write.

Conflict resolution against our PR-27528 carry, in gitops-engine/pkg/cache:
- One per-namespace SSAR helper remains: checkNamespacePermission (includes
  the API group in the review). The PR's checkPermissionForNamespace and
  handleRestrictedListError are dropped; the incremental path now runs
  through the same handleNamespacedListError policy as the full sync
  (NotFound -> skip with recorded warning, Forbidden -> SSAR, warnings
  capped), so both paths skip and report identically.
- startMissingWatches now also initializes watchCtx and namespaceCancels on
  apiMeta; upstream only does so in sync(), which would panic on the first
  incremental namespace add for an API discovered after the full sync
  (e.g. a CRD created later).
- The PR's checkPermissionForNamespace test is carried as
  Test_checkNamespacePermission_AllowedAndErrors against the kept helper.
